    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-066 — Intrinsic width for auto-width floats.** Fixes ADR-065's diagnostic finding: Wikipedia figure floats measure at 953.6px instead of ~220px, collapsing text to 22.4px (1-3 words per line).\n\n## The bug\n\nWikipedia's figure CSS:\n\n```css\nfigure[typeof~='mw:File/Thumb'] {\n    display: table;\n    float: right;\n}\n```\n\n`display: table` has no layout engine in HoneyBee (ADR-061). Figures fall back to Block, which fills parent `content_w`. The ADR-030 float probe lays out at `content_w` (976px), so `probe->width = 953.6`. Following paragraphs get `narrow_w = 976 - 953.6 = 22.4`.\n\nRoot cause measured by ADR-065 diagnostic:\n\n```\nFLOAT-L: tag=figure class=mw-default-size mw-halign-left width=953.6 accum_L=953.6\nNARROW: tag=p content_w=976.0 L=953.6 R=0.0 narrow_w=22.4\n```\n\n## The fix\n\nWhen a float has no explicit CSS `width` and its probe contains an `<img>` child with valid intrinsic dimensions, re-layout the probe at the img's width.\n\nRe-layout (not just use img_w for narrowing) so figcaption re-wraps and the float actually paints at ~220px — no overlap with the narrowed text.\n\n## What this fixes\n\n- Wikipedia figure floats (~90% of floating figures on the page) narrow at intrinsic img width\n- History section: Tim Berners-Lee photo beside readable text, not 1-3 words per line\n- ADR-063 float layout now produces usable output instead of unreadable narrow columns\n\n## What this does NOT fix\n\n- Text-only floats (`div.navbar-mini`, `side-box`) still measure at full width — needs max-content calculation (deferred)\n- `display: table` layout engine — larger ADR (ADR-067 candidate)\n- Multi-img shrink-to-fit — needs max-content\n\n## Test count\n\n- 687 → 689 cases (+2)\n- 2627 → 2633 assertions (+6)\n- Two new tests: auto-width case (> 700px), explicit-width control (600-720px)\n\n## Verification\n\n- Fixture: `docs/adr066-float-intrinsic-test.html` — 2 rows\n- Unit tests: pass\n- Wikipedia screenshot (pending): user will confirm History section renders with readable text beside the photo\n\nRefs #269\n",
